TI  - Inhibition of SIRT1 by miR-138-5p provides a mechanism for inhibiting osteoblast proliferation and promoting apoptosis under simulated microgravity.
AU  - Xu, Liqun
AU  - Zhang, Xiaoyan
AU  - Li, Gaozhi
AU  - Zhang, Lijun
AU  - Zhang, Shu
AU  - Shi, Fei
AU  - Hu, Zebing
T2  - Life sciences in space research
AB  - Microgravity can inhibit osteoblast proliferation and promote apoptosis, which is related to a reduction in mechanical stress on the bones and results in disuse  osteoporosis, but the detailed mechanism is still unclear. In this study, we  first demonstrated that miR-138-5p was upregulated, inhibited osteoblast  proliferation and induced osteoblast apoptosis under simulated microgravity.  Moreover, miR-138-5p silencing partially mitigated the effects of proliferation  and apoptosis of MC3T3-E1 cells. Our study further showed that sirtuin 1 (SIRT1)  was downregulated and negatively correlated with the expression of miR-138-5p  under simulated microgravity, which indicated that miR-138-5p inhibited  osteoblast proliferation and promoted osteoblast apoptosis by targeting SIRT1.  Thus, the miR-138-5p/SIRT1 pathway should be considered for preventative  treatment of disuse osteoporosis.
