TY  - JOUR
TI  - Astronaut adherence to exercise-based reconditioning: Psychological considerations and future directions.
AU  - McKay, Carly D.
AU  - Standage, Martyn
T2  - Musculoskeletal science & practice
AB  - INTRODUCTION: Exercise-based reconditioning is essential for mitigating the negative physiological and functional effects of spaceflight. Astronaut adherence  to prescribed reconditioning programmes is imperative, but there has been limited  research in this area. PURPOSE: This commentary discusses adherence predictors in  analogous terrestrial populations (sport, clinical rehabilitation, general  exercise) that may translate to spaceflight environments. IMPLICATIONS:  Reconditioning programmes should foster intrinsic motivation, realistic outcome  expectancies, self-regulation skills, and strong therapeutic alliances to promote  ongoing exercise adherence. Research is needed to understand spaceflight-specific  barriers and facilitators to adherence, and to develop appropriate strategies to  promote ongoing exercise behaviours.
