AB  - Research on astronaut health and model organisms have revealed six features of spaceflight biology that guide our current understanding of fundamental molecular  changes that occur during space travel. The features include oxidative stress,  DNA damage, mitochondrial dysregulation, epigenetic changes (including gene  regulation), telomere length alterations, and microbiome shifts. Here we review  the known hazards of human spaceflight, how spaceflight affects living systems  through these six fundamental features, and the associated health risks of space  exploration. We also discuss the essential issues related to the health and  safety of astronauts involved in future missions, especially planned  long-duration and Martian missions.
