TY  - JOUR
TI  - Profiling muscle transcriptome in mice exposed to microgravity using gene set enrichment analysis.
AU  - Oommen, Anup Mammen
AU  - Stafford, Phillip
AU  - Joshi, Lokesh
T2  - NPJ microgravity
AB  - Space exploration's advancement toward long-duration missions prompts intensified research on physiological effects. Despite adaptive physiological stability in  some variables, persistent changes affect genome integrity, immune response, and  cognitive function. Our study, utilizing multi-omics data from GeneLab, provides  crucial insights investigating muscle atrophy during space mission. Leveraging  NASA GeneLab's data resources, we apply systems biology-based analyses,  facilitating comprehensive understanding and enabling meta-analysis. Through  transcriptomics, we establish a reference profile of biological processes  underlying muscle atrophy, crucial for intervention development. We emphasize the  often-overlooked role of glycosylation in muscle atrophy. Our research sheds  light on fundamental molecular mechanisms, bridging gaps between space research  and terrestrial conditions. This study underscores the importance of  interdisciplinary collaboration and data-sharing initiatives like GeneLab in  advancing space medicine research.
