AU  - Rossi, Leonardo
AU  - Ciofani, Gianni
T2  - Journal of biomedical materials research. Part A
AB  - Gravity alterations elicit complex and mostly detrimental effects on biological systems. Among these, a prominent role is occupied by oxidative stress, with  consequences for tissue homeostasis and development. Studies in altered gravity  are relevant for both Earth and space biomedicine, but their implementation using  whole organisms is often troublesome. Here we utilize planarians, simple worm  model for stem cell and regeneration biology, to characterize the pathogenic  mechanisms brought by artificial gravity alterations. In particular, we provide a  comprehensive evaluation of molecular responses in intact and regenerating  specimens, and demonstrate a protective action from the space-apt for  nanotechnological antioxidant cerium oxide nanoparticles.
